  "answers": {
    "1_magnitude": "Normalized differences are smaller than C0 on average, including successful B pairs. Failure-specific extra shrinkage is not robust after controlling category, both ROI sizes and closely matching teacher margin.",
    "2_direction": "A has lower unadjusted difference cosine than B while individual cosine remains high. The effect weakens under difficulty matching; severe direction mismatch with ratio>=0.8 and cosine<0.5 affects only about 1-4.4% of Object A pairs under this exploratory threshold.",
    "3_pattern_material": "Material is somewhat more contracted in P384; both attribute types improve geometrically at 768. No robust failure-specific difference after nearest-margin matching in either type. Newer students already exceed C0 Mean Pattern AP; centered also exceeds C0 Mean Material AP in point estimate.",
    "4_resolution": "Same-pair comparison improves magnitude and direction, particularly direction for small ROIs. Roughly 41-45% of fixed P384 A pairs become correctly ranked at P768, but new failures remain; teacher head transfer recovers only about one third of residual A.",
    "5_method": "Strongest direct evidence supports testing input-detail/encoding interventions. Existing-head projections motivate discriminative diagnostics, not sufficiency of any alignment method. Relative Distillation remains a controlled-ablation hypothesis; this diagnosis does not establish an error-specific missing pair relation, AP benefit or methodological novelty."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Fixed trained models and sampled pair graph; one seed; exploratory multiple comparisons, no multiplicity correction.",
    "Nearest-margin matching is descriptive, keeps around 77% of Object A; fixed matches in bootstrap do not include rematching uncertainty.",
    "Bootstrap resamples image vertices jointly for both endpoints; no independent-pair resampling, but sparse graph/pair-selection and model-training variability are not estimated.",
    "Normalized difference norm is an angular separation; it does not measure all attribute information or irrecoverable loss.",
    "No new reader/probe was fitted, so intrinsic information availability cannot be identified."
  ]
